; The bounded memcpy/memmove -> masked load/store transform is gated on two
; things: the widest fixed-width vector register the subtarget prefers, which
; caps the bound we accept, and byte-granular masked load/store legality.
;
;   x86-64      SSE2    128-bit regs, no masked load/store -> never fires
;   x86-64-v2   SSE4.2  128-bit regs, no masked load/store -> never fires
;   x86-64-v3   AVX2    256-bit regs, but vpmaskmov handles 32/64-bit elements
;                       only, so <N x i8> is illegal       -> never fires
;   x86-64-v4   AVX512BW+VL, up to 32 bytes
;   znver4      AVX512BW+VL, up to 64 bytes
;
; The split between the last two is prefer-256-bit, which is a tuning decision
; rather than an ISA one: x86-64-v4, sapphirerapids and skylake-avx512 all set
; it and so cap getRegisterBitWidth at 256, while znver4 does not. znver4 is
; therefore the configuration that covers the 64-byte case from the bug report.

